<p>Each model, reduced to the numbers that decide whether and how it runs.
<strong>On disk</strong> is the download; <strong>streamed per token</strong> is
the weight bytes a single decoded token reads — with the KV growth it sets
generation speed on any machine (generation is memory-bound: tokens/s ≈
effective bandwidth ÷ bytes per token). <strong>KV per 1k tokens</strong> is
how the footprint grows with context; a "state" term is a recurrent
architecture's constant. <strong>Fits 8 / 16 GB</strong> allows 4k context and
~1 GB of runtime overhead.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>model</th><th>on disk</th><th>streamed per token</th>
  <th>KV per 1k tokens</th><th>fits 8 / 16 GB</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for m in models %}
    <tr><td><strong>{{ m.model }}</strong> {{ m.quant }}</td>
        <td>{{ "%.1f"|format(m.file_gb) }} GB</td>
        <td>{{ "%.1f"|format(m.body_gb) }} GB</td>
        <td>{{ "%.0f"|format(m.kv_mb_per_1k) }} MB{% if m.kv_state_mb >= 1 %} + {{ "%.0f"|format(m.kv_state_mb) }} MB state{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{{ "✓" if m.fits8 else "✗" }} / {{ "✓" if m.fits16 else "✗" }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>Measured rates below are read off the sweep curves at reference points —
how long to read a 2k / 8k prompt, and generation speed on an empty
("fresh") vs filled ("deep") context. The full curves are under
<strong>Explore</strong>; "—" means the sweep's budget ended before that
depth on that lane.</p>

<div class="cards">
{% for m in models %}
  <div class="card">
    <h3>{{ m.model }} <span class="quant">{{ m.quant }}</span></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>on disk</dt><dd>{{ "%.1f"|format(m.file_gb) }} GB</dd>
      <dt>streamed / token</dt><dd>{{ "%.1f"|format(m.body_gb) }} GB</dd>
      <dt>KV / 1k tokens</dt><dd>{{ "%.0f"|format(m.kv_mb_per_1k) }} MB</dd>
      {% if m.kv_state_mb >= 1 %}<dt>recurrent state</dt><dd>{{ "%.0f"|format(m.kv_state_mb) }} MB</dd>{% endif %}
    </dl>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>lane</th><th>2k prompt</th><th>8k prompt</th>
      <th>fresh tok/s</th><th>deep tok/s</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for a in m.anchors %}
        <tr><td>{{ a.lane }}</td><td>{{ a.t2k }}</td><td>{{ a.t8k }}</td>
            <td>{{ a.fresh }}</td><td>{{ a.deep }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {% if m.caveats %}<p class="caveat">{{ m.caveats }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
